The mouse and terminal-handling code in src/mouse/ and src/ui/suspend.ts is an
independent TypeScript implementation whose design was adapted from two
Apache-2.0 projects. No source files were copied; where a comment names a file
below, the behaviour described there was studied and re-implemented.

-------------------------------------------------------------------------------
OpenAI Codex CLI — https://github.com/openai/codex (studied at 624b45c4)
Licensed under the Apache License, Version 2.0.
Its NOTICE file reads:

  OpenAI Codex
  Copyright 2025 OpenAI

  This project includes code derived from [Ratatui](https://github.com/ratatui/ratatui), licensed under the MIT license.
  Copyright (c) 2016-2022 Florian Dehau
  Copyright (c) 2023-2025 The Ratatui Developers

Adapted ideas: the reporting-mode set and per-mode teardown with alternate
scroll off (codex-rs/tui/src/tui/alternate_screen.rs), not capturing the mouse
when tmux mouse mode is off (tui/tmux.rs), restoring the terminal before
SIGTSTP and reclaiming it on resume (tui/job_control.rs), the transcript's
wheel carry, drag selection with copy on release, multi-click word/line
selection, right-click copy and click-to-expand tool activity
(transcript_view/input.rs, transcript_view/disclosure.rs, text_selection.rs),
and the clickable "back to bottom" control (transcript_view/follow_control.rs).

-------------------------------------------------------------------------------
xAI Grok Build — https://github.com/xai-org/grok-build (studied at 2bdd1d6a)
Copyright 2023-2026 SpaceXAI. Licensed under the Apache License, Version 2.0.

Adapted ideas: scroll-stream normalisation with per-terminal events-per-notch,
wheel promotion, trackpad detection and interval-banded acceleration
(crates/codegen/xai-grok-pager-render/src/input/mouse.rs), reassembling mouse
reports split across reads (xai-grok-pager/src/app/csi_filter.rs and
x10_filter.rs), re-asserting capture on focus-in (app/event_loop.rs), one
shared teardown for exit, signals and crashes (app/terminal_restore.rs), a
runtime mouse-reporting toggle (slash/commands/toggle_mouse_reporting.rs),
and staying inline under Zellij.

